// CLAIM: Smaller shape decisions
// HOLDS: refused
// REFUSED-BECAUSE: `%` is the percent literal
// NOTE: this line used to read `unexpected character: '%'`, and the gate caught the change the day
//       the message was improved — which is the branch working rather than a nuisance. The CLAIM
//       did not move: `%` is still not modulo. Only what the compiler says about it did.
// WHY: stands for the group. `%` is the percent literal, never modulo — the one most likely to
//      be added by somebody who missed the reason.
region main {
    let left: Int = 7 % 2;
    print("{left}");
}
